claim.claim-text:
a display (160);
a memory (130);
a wireless communication circuitry (190) configured to support a wireless fidelity, Wi-Fi, Direct protocol; and
a processor (120) operatively connected with the memory (130), and the wireless communication circuitry (190),
wherein the processor (120) is configured to:

perform wireless communication with an external electronic device based on a first channel attribute, via the wireless communication circuitry (190), the first channel attribute including at least one of a frequency band or a bandwidth;
detect that an event associated with power save occurs;
in response to detection of the event associated with power save, transmit a first request message requesting to change the first channel attribute to a second channel attribute, at least a portion of which differs from the first channel attribute, to the external electronic device via the wireless communication circuitry (190);
receive a first response message from the external electronic device via the wireless communication circuitry (190); and
in response to the first response, perform the wireless communication with the external electronic device based on the second channel attribute,
wherein wireless communication based on the frequency band or the bandwidth included in the second channel attribute consumes power less than power consumed by wireless communication based on the frequency band or the bandwidth included in the first channel attribute.

detect that the event associated with the power save ends;
transmit a second request message requesting to change the second channel attribute to the first channel attribute to the external electronic device, via the wireless communication circuitry (190);
receive a second response message from the external electronic device via the wireless communication circuitry (190); and
in response to the second response, perform the wireless communication with the external electronic device based on the first channel attribute.

performing wireless communication with an external electronic device based on a first channel attribute including at least one of a frequency band and a bandwidth;
detecting that an event associated with power save occurs;
transmitting a first request message requesting to change the first channel attribute to a second channel attribute, at least a portion of which differs from the first channel attribute, to the external electronic device based on the event;
receiving a first response message from the external electronic device; and
in response to the first response, performing the wireless communication with the external electronic device based on the second channel attribute,
wherein wireless communication based on the frequency band or the bandwidth included in the second channel attribute consumes power less than power consumed by wireless communication based on the frequency band or the bandwidth included in the first channel attribute.

detecting that a data rate of a transmit signal or a receive signal between the electronic device and the external electronic device is less than a threshold during a specified time;
detecting that a screen of a display of the electronic device changes from an on-state to an off-state; or
detecting that an application run in the electronic device and the external electronic device ends or pauses.

detecting that the event associated with the power save ends;
transmitting a second request message requesting to change the second channel attribute to the first channel attribute to the external electronic device;
receiving a second response message from the external electronic device; and
in response to the second response, performing the wireless communication with the external electronic device based on the first channel attribute.
